---
/**
 * @category FAQ
 * @theme starquix
 * @name FAQ
 */
---
<section class='bg-stone-50 px-4 py-20 md:px-10 md:py-28 xl:px-16 xl:py-32 dark:bg-stone-900'>
  <div class='grid grid-cols-1 gap-12 xl:grid-cols-12 xl:gap-8'>
    <div class='flex flex-col gap-5 md:flex-row md:items-end md:justify-between md:gap-10 xl:col-span-4 xl:flex-col xl:items-start xl:justify-start xl:gap-6'>
      <h2 class='m-0 font-sans text-[2.75rem] font-semibold leading-[0.95] tracking-[-0.04em] text-stone-900 text-balance md:text-6xl xl:text-[4rem] dark:text-stone-50'>Questions</h2>
      <div class='flex flex-col gap-3 md:max-w-sm'>
        <p class='m-0 font-sans text-lg leading-relaxed text-stone-600 text-pretty dark:text-stone-400'>Answers about building, importing and publishing a site with Starquix.</p>
        <p class='m-0 font-sans text-sm leading-normal text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400'>Something else? <a href='#' class='font-medium text-stone-900 underline underline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-stone-900 dark:text-stone-50 dark:focus-visible:outline-stone-50'>Write to support</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class='flex flex-col border-0 border-b border-solid border-stone-200 xl:col-span-8 dark:border-stone-700'>
      <details class='group border-0 border-t border-solid border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700' open>
        <summary class='flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-6 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-stone-900 dark:focus-visible:outline-stone-50 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden'>
          <h3 class='m-0 font-sans text-lg font-semibold text-stone-900 md:text-xl dark:text-stone-50'>Do I need to know how to code?</h3>
          <svg class='mt-0.5 size-6 shrink-0 text-stone-900 transition-transform duration-200 ease-out group-open:rotate-45 dark:text-stone-50' viewBox='0 0 24 24' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-linecap='round' aria-hidden='true'><path d='M12 5v14M5 12h14' /></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class='m-0 max-w-[40rem] pb-6 pr-12 font-sans text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 text-pretty dark:text-stone-400'>No. You add sections, edit text in place and change spacing, color and type in the Design panel. If you do write code, open the same files in your editor and Starquix picks up the changes.</p>
      </details>
      <details class='group border-0 border-t border-solid border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700'>
        <summary class='flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-6 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-stone-900 dark:focus-visible:outline-stone-50 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden'>
          <h3 class='m-0 font-sans text-lg font-semibold text-stone-900 md:text-xl dark:text-stone-50'>Can I import a site I already built with Astro?</h3>
          <svg class='mt-0.5 size-6 shrink-0 text-stone-900 transition-transform duration-200 ease-out group-open:rotate-45 dark:text-stone-50' viewBox='0 0 24 24' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-linecap='round' aria-hidden='true'><path d='M12 5v14M5 12h14' /></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class='m-0 max-w-[40rem] pb-6 pr-12 font-sans text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 text-pretty dark:text-stone-400'>Yes. Choose Import and pick the project folder. Starquix works on a copy, keeps your pages and components, and opens Markdown pages as MDX so you can edit them on the canvas.</p>
      </details>
      <details class='group border-0 border-t border-solid border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700'>
        <summary class='flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-6 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-stone-900 dark:focus-visible:outline-stone-50 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden'>
          <h3 class='m-0 font-sans text-lg font-semibold text-stone-900 md:text-xl dark:text-stone-50'>Where are my files kept?</h3>
          <svg class='mt-0.5 size-6 shrink-0 text-stone-900 transition-transform duration-200 ease-out group-open:rotate-45 dark:text-stone-50' viewBox='0 0 24 24' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-linecap='round' aria-hidden='true'><path d='M12 5v14M5 12h14' /></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class='m-0 max-w-[40rem] pb-6 pr-12 font-sans text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 text-pretty dark:text-stone-400'>On your Mac, in a regular Astro project folder. Commit it to Git, open it in any code editor or export it as a zip whenever you like.</p>
      </details>
      <details class='group border-0 border-t border-solid border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700'>
        <summary class='flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-6 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-stone-900 dark:focus-visible:outline-stone-50 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden'>
          <h3 class='m-0 font-sans text-lg font-semibold text-stone-900 md:text-xl dark:text-stone-50'>How do I publish to my own domain?</h3>
          <svg class='mt-0.5 size-6 shrink-0 text-stone-900 transition-transform duration-200 ease-out group-open:rotate-45 dark:text-stone-50' viewBox='0 0 24 24' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-linecap='round' aria-hidden='true'><path d='M12 5v14M5 12h14' /></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class='m-0 max-w-[40rem] pb-6 pr-12 font-sans text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 text-pretty dark:text-stone-400'>Press Publish and Starquix builds and deploys the site. On the Pro plan, add your domain in the publish settings and point its DNS records to the address shown there.</p>
      </details>
      <details class='group border-0 border-t border-solid border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700'>
        <summary class='flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-6 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-stone-900 dark:focus-visible:outline-stone-50 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden'>
          <h3 class='m-0 font-sans text-lg font-semibold text-stone-900 md:text-xl dark:text-stone-50'>Which versions of Astro and Tailwind are supported?</h3>
          <svg class='mt-0.5 size-6 shrink-0 text-stone-900 transition-transform duration-200 ease-out group-open:rotate-45 dark:text-stone-50' viewBox='0 0 24 24' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-linecap='round' aria-hidden='true'><path d='M12 5v14M5 12h14' /></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class='m-0 max-w-[40rem] pb-6 pr-12 font-sans text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 text-pretty dark:text-stone-400'>New projects start on Astro 7 with Tailwind CSS 3.4. Imported sites keep the Astro and Tailwind versions they already use.</p>
      </details>
      <details class='group border-0 border-t border-solid border-stone-200 dark:border-stone-700'>
        <summary class='flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 py-6 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-stone-900 dark:focus-visible:outline-stone-50 [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden'>
          <h3 class='m-0 font-sans text-lg font-semibold text-stone-900 md:text-xl dark:text-stone-50'>What happens to my site if I cancel?</h3>
          <svg class='mt-0.5 size-6 shrink-0 text-stone-900 transition-transform duration-200 ease-out group-open:rotate-45 dark:text-stone-50' viewBox='0 0 24 24' fill='none' stroke='currentColor' stroke-width='1.5' stroke-linecap='round' aria-hidden='true'><path d='M12 5v14M5 12h14' /></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class='m-0 max-w-[40rem] pb-6 pr-12 font-sans text-base leading-relaxed text-stone-600 text-pretty dark:text-stone-400'>It stays online on a Starquix subdomain, and the project folder stays on your Mac. Custom domains come back when you upgrade again.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
